[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     14[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     15[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * **Runtime options / modes / flags axis: EMPTY.** Nothing can be configured.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     16[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * **Entry-point axis: a single function.** It is simultaneously the lowest-level
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     17[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   and the only-level API — there is no convenience wrapper to mistake for the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     18[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   real thing. Every row below therefore drives `float2half` directly through the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     19[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `.so` export.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     20[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     21[0m:[38;5;10m[49m The only axes that remain are the **input-shape** axes, and the C code
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     22[0m:[38;5;10m[49m distinguishes them purely through its two lookup tables. Those distinctions were
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     23[0m:[38;5;10m[49m extracted mechanically by run-length-encoding `m__shift[512]` and reading the
